## Section 2: Certification

I certify that I am not a party to a malign foreign talent recruitment program as defined in Section 10632 of the CHIPS and Science Act of 2022.

---

## Section 3: Definition Reference

A **malign foreign talent recruitment program** (MFTRP), as defined in 42 USC 19237, is any program organized by a **foreign country of concern** — the People's Republic of China (PRC), the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (DPRK), the Russian Federation, or the Islamic Republic of Iran — or an entity substantially funded by or subject to the direction of such a country, that recruits science and technology professionals to: (a) transfer knowledge or research funded by the United States Government; (b) acquire proprietary information, trade secrets, or intellectual property without proper authorization; or (c) compromise the integrity of the United States research enterprise through undisclosed conflicts of interest or commitment.

> **Note**: Pakistan is NOT designated as a "foreign country of concern" under the CHIPS and Science Act of 2022 and therefore is not subject to MFTRP restrictions under this certification.

